d3987f6da68e373928da96eb653423d86d2bb52a1fb1599c98eec53a4ff", "source_label": "descent-lemma-descent-data-sheaves", "usage": "descent-sheaf-set-matrices", "usage_source": {"after": "\n\\end{matrix}", "before": "F", "environments": ["matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "descent-representable", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 297, "start": 280}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0008", "source": " is representable"}], "source": "$$\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{descent data }(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})\\text{ such that}\\\\\n\\text{each }X_i \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_\\tau)\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{sheaves }F\\text{ on }(\\Sch/S)_\\tau\\text{ such that}\\\\\n\\text{each }h_{S_i} \\times F\\text{ is representable}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}.\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 734, "start": 410}, "source_hash": "sha256:2727b52f174d8872331d641dfa1c84bbb4bec743947de3c523ce6d75015606f2"}], "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02W4", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})\\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "}\\\\\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "}X_i \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_\\tau)\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0005": "}F\\text{", "MATHSEG_0006": "}(\\Sch/S)_\\tau\\text{", "MATHSEG_0007": "}\\\\\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0008": "}h_{S_i} \\times F\\text{", "MATHSEG_0009": "}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}.\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$\\tau \\in \\{Zariski, fppf, \\etale, smooth, syntomic\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$S \\in \\Ob(\\Sch_\\tau)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{S_i \\to S\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0007": "$h_{S_i} \\times F$", "MATH_0008": "$X_i$", "MATH_0009": "$F$", "MATH_0010": "$(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-fpqc}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descent-data-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6298268f6bb6fbefb46cf578a8016f8e435aa9757ccbb7c10c022e701f083cf4", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:9850cba6636091990b4b0a51deda4e607d6d6c6fc063185dad26e4ccd1d12451", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:efe99b099f8ee9367dcb83c53643d506a0d859554a53e83796c938d6147d50b0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>The\nfact that fpqc is missing is not a typo. See discussion\nin Topologies, Section <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a big <MATH_0003>-site.\nLet <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a covering in the\nsite <MATH_0006>. There is an equivalence of\ncategories\n<MATHSEG_0001>descent data <MATHSEG_0002> such that<MATHSEG_0003>each <MATHSEG_0004>sheaves <MATHSEG_0005> on <MATHSEG_0006> such that<MATHSEG_0007>each <MATHSEG_0008> is representable<MATHSEG_0009>\nMoreover,\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the objects representing <MATH_0007> on the right hand side\ncorrespond to the schemes <MATH_0008> on the left hand side, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the sheaf <MATH_0009> is representable if and only if the\ncorresponding descent datum <MATH_0010> is effective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be18a0db18331830f09b5e2bb97c5e0e0e8bc038a86e2ab789b1dd0523a21bb2", "unit_id": "tag:02W5:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02W4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$h_{S_i} \\times F$", "MATH_0005": "$X_i$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0007": "$X_i \\to S_i$", "MATH_0008": "$X_i \\times_S S_{i'}$", "MATH_0009": "$S_i \\times_S X_{i'}$", "MATH_0010": "$h_{S_i} \\times F \\times h_{S_{i'}}$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\varphi_{ii'} : X_i \\times_S S_{i'} \\to S_i \\times_S X_{i'}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\varphi_{ii'}$", "MATH_0013": "$S_i \\times_S S_{i'}$", "MATH_0014": "$F \\mapsto (X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})$", "MATH_0015": "$i$", "MATH_0016": "$F_i$", "MATH_0017": "$h_{X_i}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\varphi_{ii'}$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\varphi_{ii'} :\nF_i \\times h_{S_{i'}}\n\\longrightarrow\nh_{S_i} \\times F_{i'}\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$h_{S_i} \\times h_{S_{i'}}$", "MATH_0021": "$F$", "MATH_0022": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\coprod_{i, i'} F_i \\times h_{S_{i'}}\n\\ar@<1ex>[rr]^-{\\text{pr}_0}\n\\ar@<-1ex>[rr]_-{\\text{pr}_1 \\circ \\varphi_{ii'}}\n& &\n\\coprod_i F_i \\ar[r]\n&\nF\n}\n$$", "MATH_0023": "$h_{S_i} \\times F$", "MATH_0024": "$F_i$", "MATH_0025": "$(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'}) \\mapsto F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-fpqc-universal-effective-epimorphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-yoneda}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0005": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0006": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:aab0a6b8ef4d2828b347a77210ed86ace154d77270081ab35599d60ed8d83608", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0991f4a5d8db088f02bf14f835c627724b1a654df58345ea9df93ffa7f4c1445", "source_text": "We have seen in Section <REF_0001>\nthat representable presheaves are sheaves on the site <MATH_0001>.\nMoreover, the Yoneda lemma (Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nguarantees that maps between representable\nsheaves correspond one to one with maps between the representing objects.\nWe will use these remarks without further mention during the proof.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet us construct the functor from right to left.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf on <MATH_0003> such that each\n<MATH_0004> is representable. In this case let <MATH_0005>\nbe a representing object in <MATH_0006>.\nIt comes equipped with a morphism <MATH_0007>.\nThen both <MATH_0008> and <MATH_0009>\nrepresent the sheaf <MATH_0010>\nand hence we obtain an isomorphism\n<MATH_0011>\nIt is straightforward to see that the maps <MATH_0012>\nare morphisms over <MATH_0013> and satisfy the\ncocycle condition. The functor from right to left is given\nby this construction <MATH_0014>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nLet us construct a functor from left to right.\nFor each <MATH_0015> denote <MATH_0016> the sheaf <MATH_0017>.\nThe isomorphisms <MATH_0018> give isomorphisms\n<MATH_0019>\nover <MATH_0020>.\nSet <MATH_0021> equal to the coequalizer in the following diagram\n<MATH_0022>\nThe cocycle condition guarantees that <MATH_0023> is\nisomorphic to <MATH_0024> and hence representable.\nThe functor from left to right is given\nby this construction <MATH_0025>.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nWe omit the verification that these constructions\nare mutually quasi-inverse functors. The final statements\n(1) and (2) follow from the constructions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e9a5b3afeb2f147f667645a731a3a18d19d91639db3c3720e7c24eaab12a34c4", "unit_id": "tag:02W5:proof"}
